    {
      "title": "Quality of Life and New Player Improvements",
      "anchor": "Quality_of_Life_and_New_Player_Improvements",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Graphical settings will automatically adjust for new PC players based on their system performance"
            },
            {
              "text": "Players will now auto-bypass the login screen if the servers are active; we saved you a click every time you log in!"
            },
            {
              "text": "Players’ last-played queue will now be remembered in online settings. If you last played Joust on PC and then go to play on Xbox, Joust should be the selected queue."
            },
            {
              "text": "Added a button to Close the Settings menu"
            },
            {
              "text": "Several Match Lobby clean-ups have been made for better clarity:",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Activate Boost is only visible in Assault"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Change Role is only visible in Conquest"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Role Tabs are only visible in Conquest"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Owned Gods are always sorted to the top of the list"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Added a button to close the filter tab"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Aspects are disabled until a player reaches Account Level 5",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Aspects are generally slightly more complicated or slightly more niche than a God’s core kit. We want to make sure players are a little more comfortable with SMITE before introducing the idea of Aspects."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Players will automatically Autobuild (including a Relic selection) until reaching Account Level 5",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Similarly, forcing new players to click through selecting an Autobuild (or accidentally turning on Manual Build) and Relic was unnecessary complexity at this point in their learning journey."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Relic descriptions on the pre-game Relic Selection Screen have been simplified",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "This text is intended to help players quickly understand and decide which Relic to purchase. The full text is still available via tooltips."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Help Text should now be more obvious",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "The old color treatment was very easy for new players to miss"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "New Players will default to a new “Action Camera” perspective",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "We believe that new players will be better served by a camera with a narrower FOV, which makes targets in front of them appear bigger and allows combat to be easier to read"
                },
                {
                  "text": "This should not affect current players, who may prefer the wider FOV currently used, which allows you to see more happening off to the sides at the expense of making things in front of you smaller"
                },
                {
                  "text": "This is just the first test of this camera, and further changes may occur"
                },
                {
                  "text": "If you want to change your camera setting, go to Settings > Gameplay and find Action Camera at the bottom of the list"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Added “Good for New Players” tags to the Free Rotation Gods"
            },
            {
              "text": "Number Summing",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "If a single ability deals multiple instances of damage, those damage numbers will now add together"
                },
                {
                  "text": "For example: If Anubis 1 deals 30 damage per tick, it will show 30, then 60, then 90 instead of showing 30 three times"
                },
                {
                  "text": "This can be disabled in Settings"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Directional Damage Indicators",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "A red arrow will appear on the HUD and point towards Gods when they damage you"
                },
                {
                  "text": "The size of this arrow is scaled to the damage dealt, and will increase in size as you are dealt additional damage"
                },
                {
                  "text": "This can be disabled in Settings"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "subsections": []
    },
